{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends","id":1500845,"title":"What are we expecting in Crucible of Legends","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-20T09:18:56-08:00","id":1500845,"title":"What are we expecting in Crucible of Legends","content":"Sorry if this has been clarified elsewhere, I couldn't find a reasonably recent thread on this.<br /> <br /> What kind of outline or hints have we had for the contents of the long awaited storyteller guide? <br /> <br /> I'm looking to start a lunar game this year and wondering if it would be worth waiting for its release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T23:08:05-08:00","id":1500900,"title":"","content":"I went through and compiled a bunch of things mentioned on the discord awhile back. This is a cursory and incomplete list, but it was confirmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Specific Lore and QCs for all 10 mainline exalted<br /> -Alternate subsystems and fixes including a venture-shaped project system, alternate craft, fixes to sail and alternate stunt rules.<br /> -Teamwork Rules<br /> -Alternate Flat XP costs<br /> -Optional rules for Virtues<br /> -Rules Hacks for Limit<br /> - quick resolution for one-sided combat<br /> -Discussion of Exalted naming conventions.<br /> -A discussion of handling themes of empire and slavery<br /> -discussion of existing mechanics and how to phase them in slowly<br /> -At least as much advice for running chronicles as Essence has, probably more (including session 0)<br /> -Advice on adjudicating the rules and changing them on the fly<br /> -Adjusting tone and the presence of magic and exalts in the setting<br /> -A discussion on the otherworlds in broad strokes, along with major actors in the setting<br /> -A deeper look at QC design\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26927-sylvanvixen","name":"SylvanVixen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T00:27:28-08:00","id":1500905,"title":"","content":"It's really that 'at least as much advice for running chronicles as Essence' part that I hope they go crazy in-depth into. Exalted has been almost deliberately difficult to run for pretty much its entire lifespan as a game, and Crucible might actually make things easier for one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T03:39:55-08:00","id":1500914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SylvanVixen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1500900#post1500900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went through and compiled a bunch of things mentioned on the discord awhile back. This is a cursory and incomplete list, but it was confirmed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've also have confirmation on discussion of RPG safety tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T07:27:54-08:00","id":1501031,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers guys!<br /> <br /> I was really hoping to hear that we would be getting alternatives for some of the subsystems, flat XP is a big boon too. Sounds like it will definitely be worth the wait.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> sorry if I'm being dense here, but what do you mean by RPG safety tools? Are we talking like the Red Rule and other such concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T09:03:40-08:00","id":1501038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1501031#post1501031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> sorry if I'm being dense here, but what do you mean by RPG safety tools? Are we talking like the Red Rule and other such concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, safety tools is the commonly applied term for props and practices that a group might adopt that would allow somebody to put the brakes on if the Storyteller or another player is taking things in a direction that cross their boundaries. Things like X-cards and the like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T00:51:28-08:00","id":1501124,"title":"","content":"Yeah, also, discussion of how to handle themes of empire and slavery seems like it'd intersect with lines and veils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T14:14:14-08:00","id":1501570,"title":"","content":"I'm really interested to see some discussion of the Exalted naming conventions.<br /> <br /> A persistent issue I've seen over the years is that Exalted draws a lot from Wuxia including some naming conventions, but a lot of players don't know what courtesy names or art names are (it's improved a lot since Thunderbolt Fantasy). As such there's been some<i> really weird</i> underlying assumptions about Creation's given names, the cumulation in a thaumaturgy ritual called First Greeting that asks the Maidens for the name most appropriate for a newborn determined by their destiny so essentially we ended up with magic naming ceremonies all over the Threshold, rather than the occam's razor solution that <i>people sometimes change their name. </i>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:23:30-08:00","id":1502155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1501570#post1501570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really interested to see some discussion of the Exalted naming conventions.<br /> <br /> A persistent issue I've seen over the years is that Exalted draws a lot from Wuxia including some naming conventions, but a lot of players don't know what courtesy names or art names are (it's improved a lot since Thunderbolt Fantasy). As such there's been some<i> really weird</i> underlying assumptions about Creation's given names, the cumulation in a thaumaturgy ritual called First Greeting that asks the Maidens for the name most appropriate for a newborn determined by their destiny so essentially we ended up with magic naming ceremonies all over the Threshold, rather than the occam's razor solution that <i>people sometimes change their name. </i>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, having had an awesome prophetic name from birth just feels way cooler then admitting you went and changed your name to something fitting your career path after the fact. At least it does to me, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:57:31-08:00","id":1502160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1502155#post1502155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fairness, having had an awesome prophetic name from birth just feels way cooler then admitting you went and changed your name to something fitting your career path after the fact. At least it does to me, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though a prophesised name kind of creates a scenario where people are put in boxes defining their life from the word go, whereas changing one's name as an adjustment to circumstances both conveys personal agency and is more of an ongoing conversation between oneself and one's culture.<br /> <br /> I think it helps to be familiar with the range of real life societies in which taking different names at different stages of life is totally unexceptional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T16:24:00-08:00","id":1502165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1502160#post1502160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though a prophesised name kind of creates a scenario where people are put in boxes defining their life from the word go, whereas changing one's name as an adjustment to circumstances both conveys personal agency and is more of an ongoing conversation between oneself and one's culture.<br /> <br /> I think it helps to be familiar with the range of real life societies in which taking different names at different stages of life is totally unexceptional.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, there are cultures where people change names as a matter of course during coming of age ceremonies and that kind of thing. But that also hits differently then the concept of an 'art name' that was mentioned (I think it might be similar to the concept of a courtesy name, though?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T17:30:39-08:00","id":1502171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1502155#post1502155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fairness, having had an awesome prophetic name from birth just feels way cooler then admitting you went and changed your name to something fitting your career path after the fact. At least it does to me, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally find the insistence that Invincible Sword Princess was called that as a baby to be very silly. I wouldn't stop someone having a prophetic name but the way that ritual casually normalised them felt like erasure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T19:46:12-08:00","id":1502175,"title":"","content":"I don't mind a ritual like that, but it should be pretty rare. Like most people, even most nobles, never have that ritual performed on them because it's so rare to find someone who can use it. And, of course, there are a lot of frauds out there who will claim that they know how to learn someone's prophetic name, and it's all bullshit. But occasionally you have someone who really does have a prophetic name, and that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:02:31-08:00","id":1502356,"title":"","content":"I want confirmation about definitive articles in Abyssal titles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for RPG safety tools, the generic trio are Lines, Veils, and the X-card. Veils are the things that you\u2019re okay with having in the game, but don\u2019t want to focus on. It\u2019s the very classic fade-to-black. Lines are the things that you just don\u2019t want. No rape, no torture, etc. The X-card is a player tool to signal that you\u2019re done with this scene, that something\u2019s bothering you. You show the card, your GM sees it, and quickly draws the scene to a close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T12:03:37-08:00","id":1502947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1501570#post1501570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really interested to see some discussion of the Exalted naming conventions.<br /> <br /> A persistent issue I've seen over the years is that Exalted draws a lot from Wuxia including some naming conventions, but a lot of players don't know what courtesy names or art names are (it's improved a lot since Thunderbolt Fantasy). As such there's been some<i> really weird</i> underlying assumptions about Creation's given names, the cumulation in a thaumaturgy ritual called First Greeting that asks the Maidens for the name most appropriate for a newborn determined by their destiny so essentially we ended up with magic naming ceremonies all over the Threshold, rather than the occam's razor solution that <i>people sometimes change their name. </i>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It has similar energy to this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Sidereals page 227</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>TOO PERFECT</b><br /> Sometimes things in the world of Exalted seem just too perfect, or even contrived. The Exalt Panther has an anima banner that looks like a panther, even though he possessed that<br /> name long before his Exaltation. The Bull of the North\u2019s anima resembles a mighty bull, and he\u2019s the greatest warlord of the North; and the god of war of the South so happens to be a god of cattle.<br /> Though many had reason to recall it, everyone forgot the name of the Scarlet Empress. Of course, these are elements of storytelling, but they are also evidence of the Bureau of Destiny at work. The Exalted may bend, or even break, the fate held in store for them, but they are already shaped by it before the Exaltation even occurs. For the Storyteller, this can be a gift\u2014if some aspect of your series seems just too perfect, then perhaps Heaven wanted it that way.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't a good thing, there's much simpler explanations to all 3 of these that don't require Heaven becoming involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 02-13-2023, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T15:36:45-08:00","id":1502964,"title":"","content":"Yeah, those ones read as super weird.<br /> <br /> &quot;Panther has an anima banner that looks like a panther. Coincidence? I think not!&quot;<br /> &quot;Maybe the anima took that form on purpose to match his name.&quot;<br /> &quot;Shut up! And what about the Bull of the North? Some guy getting that nickname who just so happens to be a really great warlord, and who would have thought it, there's a war god who is also a bull!&quot;<br /> &quot;Doesn't that just means that these are societies with a reason to consider bulls as symbolic of war?&quot;<br /> &quot;SHUT UP!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T07:30:19-08:00","id":1503026,"title":"","content":"The idea that Panther and Swan were named <i>after</i> their anima banners rather than those being a reflection of they are is pretty cursed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1502356#post1502356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for RPG safety tools, the generic trio are Lines, Veils, and the X-card. Veils are the things that you\u2019re okay with having in the game, but don\u2019t want to focus on. It\u2019s the very classic fade-to-black. Lines are the things that you just don\u2019t want. No rape, no torture, etc. The X-card is a player tool to signal that you\u2019re done with this scene, that something\u2019s bothering you. You show the card, your GM sees it, and quickly draws the scene to a close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently its covering more than just the basics. I asked about that specifically because I'm writing a guide on sex and gender for Ex3 and have a fairly detailed section on safety tools given the subject matter and well, now I find myself at a bit of an impasse until I've seen what Crucible has to say.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T09:07:09-08:00","id":1503038,"title":"","content":"It has never been specify so I\u2019m wondering if an Exalted\u2019s choice of anima banner is a (sub)conscious decision. But since exalting tends to happen in dangerous or stressful situations, choosing the shape of your glowing thing doesn\u2019t sound quite possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T13:55:30-08:00","id":1503063,"title":"","content":"They reflect their bearers. The weird thought here, for me, is why people would feel weird about banners that... reflect their bearers. <br /> Something like Panther having a panther in his anima is all but expected. Because, surprise surprise, people have plenty values derived from external attributes, like a given name, its symbolism and the various semiotics from whatever cultures they have absorbed. <i>Of course</i> Panther's anima banner would have a panther in it. It doesn't have to, but everything is in place for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T13:58:57-08:00","id":1503064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1503026#post1503026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Panther and Swan were named <i>after</i> their anima banners rather than those being a reflection of they are is pretty cursed.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>For the curse of it, I believe that's what really happened. I guess those names are just like Nicknames or Aliases... they want to hide their original name for protection or for the sake of their family or something like that? Maybe they don't mind using those new names.<br /> <br /> After exaltation they became &quot;Anathema&quot;, only later they understood that they were Solars (except Panther for Zenith reasons). That is &quot;a new life&quot; so I will bear a new name... and that name is most likely to be your Anima Banner.<br /> <br /> <b><i>- OMG look at that pilar of light! That's were the Panther Anathema is, lets run from it before he see us!</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> - 5 Magic Materials BeamKlaves and Gyroscopic Chakrans ? OK<br /> - Autochthonia updated World Map? OK<br /> And many more! <a href=\"http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals\" target=\"_blank\">http://efq.deviantart.com/gallery/48131405/Alchemicals</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2498-yukiartic","name":"Yukiartic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T04:32:11-08:00","id":1503128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yukiartic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1503064#post1503064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the curse of it, I believe that's what really happened. I guess those names are just like Nicknames or Aliases... they want to hide their original name for protection or for the sake of their family or something like that? Maybe they don't mind using those new names.<br /> <br /> After exaltation they became &quot;Anathema&quot;, only later they understood that they were Solars (except Panther for Zenith reasons). That is &quot;a new life&quot; so I will bear a new name... and that name is most likely to be your Anima Banner.<br /> <br /> <b><i>- OMG look at that pilar of light! That's were the Panther Anathema is, lets run from it before he see us!</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually my issue.<br /> <br /> I've said earlier in this thread that I'm fine with someone changing their name after Exaltation. What I find cursed are the implications of the Too Perfect sidebar and the ritual First Greeting, that those names were pre-ordained by destiny itself to fit their animas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T08:10:45-08:00","id":1503139,"title":"","content":"I feel the notion of putting out there a concept that sometimes things rhyming in certain ways or coming across as narratively convenient might be proof of Heavens subtle influence is fine, its just that the given examples come across as bizare/unnecessary because there is plenty of good reason for them already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T09:03:37-08:00","id":1503144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1503128#post1503128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not actually my issue.<br /> <br /> I've said earlier in this thread that I'm fine with someone changing their name after Exaltation. What I find cursed are the implications of the Too Perfect sidebar and the ritual First Greeting, that those names were pre-ordained by destiny itself to fit their animas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animas that have been known to change between holders of the same Exaltation, too. Was there some kind of assumption that the anima banner never changed between them that went into this sidebar? I have been intensely confused at the intent and assumptions that went into it for the past 16 years. Do people actually run their Creation that way? Baffling, if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T16:38:37-08:00","id":1503185,"title":"","content":"I assume it's mostly that Exalted 2e writer need to reconcile any apparent inconsistency &quot;how can the anima be a reflection of Panther if it was a panther for the Hierophant too?&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T13:03:46-07:00","id":1519354,"title":"","content":"Have we had it conclusively ruled that solar exaltations retain their caste from one incarnation to the next, nevermind specific anima banners?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T15:06:55-07:00","id":1519369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1519354#post1519354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we had it conclusively ruled that solar exaltations retain their caste from one incarnation to the next, nevermind specific anima banners?</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have to an extent said they assume yes, but won't put it in text in case that's something you'd rather not worry about for your table.<br /> <br /> Animas retaining has been mostly something only demonstrated by a specific author though. In general that is personal to the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T07:08:53-07:00","id":1519423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1519354#post1519354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have we had it conclusively ruled that solar exaltations retain their caste from one incarnation to the next, nevermind specific anima banners?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i don't think that we've enen been specifically told that the anima banners are never subject to change even for the same person. A banner represents the person, so it would not be out of the question for it to change if something major, something that significantly redefined who they are, happened to the person. And i don't remember ever reading this is flat out impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":434,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","user":"Astralporing","date":". 08-02-2023, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:34:13-07:00","id":1519491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500845-what-are-we-expecting-in-crucible-of-legends?p=1519423#post1519423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, i don't think that we've enen been specifically told that the anima banners are never subject to change even for the same person. A banner represents the person, so it would not be out of the question for it to change if something major, something that significantly redefined who they are, happened to the person. And i don't remember ever reading this is flat out impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't. There is a thing where in <i>Dreams of the First Age</i>, the Solars share their animas wiht the sig' characters they are predecessors of, but that seems to be a particular thing of that author. It is not repeated with the Sidereals or Lunars. And some of the characters both in that book and <i>Scroll of Heroes</i> indeed have different animas. Notably Kejak goes from &quot;A rich, soothing green&quot; to &quot;A hard, crystline green&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T12:52:59-07:00","id":1519496,"title":"","content":"Though it is worth noting that your Banner can change over time, if significant changes to your personality or major life-changling events occur. Like, say, orchestrating the downfall of your civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}